clean all-three games: 5,333 (386 date clusters)
price correlations: K-book=0.9987  P-book=0.9968  K-P=0.9969

=== separability: how much of each exchange price is not the book? ===
  exchange      R2 on book  idiosyncratic  residual coef       z       p
  Kalshi            0.9946          0.54%          1.282   +2.11   0.035
  Polymarket        0.9865          1.35%          0.380   +1.13   0.259
  Read carefully, in both directions. A high R2 is NOT evidence that an
  exchange copies the book: two independent, equally accurate forecasters
  of the SAME games are also ~0.99 correlated, because the games differ
  enormously in difficulty and both track the truth. Equally, the small
  idiosyncratic share means the lead-lag nulls elsewhere in this project
  cannot separate parallel discovery from same-step mirroring — a maker
  quoting continuously off the book produces no lead at any resolution.
  What the design CAN say is below (does the residual inform?) and in
  niche_gradient (are exchanges calibrated where no book exists at all?).

